se_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "884c56d5f217782d1097ed06237fe2ab45675e0787500cf701f35dd3b22d35a3" "basis" 1560 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103989" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "884c56d5f217782d1097ed06237fe2ab45675e0787500cf701f35dd3b22d35a3" "basis" 1560 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103989" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "884c56d5f217782d1097ed06237fe2ab45675e0787500cf701f35dd3b22d35a3" "basis" 1560 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate\n${\\int }_{4}^{11}\\frac{14}{5{x}^{2}+16x+3}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "884c56d5f217782d1097ed06237fe2ab45675e0787500cf701f35dd3b22d35a3" "basis" 1560 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We'll work out the indefinite integral first and then proceed with the definite integral.\n\nFirst, we note that a denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n5{x}^{2}+16x+3=(5x+1)(x+3).\n$$\n\nSo the integrand can be converted into a sum of partial fractions,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{14}{5{x}^{2}+16x+3} & =\\frac{14}{(5x+1)(x+3)}=\\frac{A}{(5x+1)}+\\frac{B}{(x+3)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n14=A(x+3)+B(5x+1).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-3,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14 & =A(-3+3)+B(5(-3)+1) \\\\ 14 & =-14B \\\\ B & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-\\frac{1}{5},$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14 & =A(-\\frac{1}{5}+3)+B(5(-\\frac{1}{5})+1) \\\\ 14 & =\\frac{14}{5}A \\\\ A & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{14}{5{x}^{2}+16x+3}=\\frac{5}{5x+1}-\\frac{1}{(x+3)}.\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{14}{5{x}^{2}+16x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{5}{5x+1}-\\frac{1}{x+3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{5}{5x+1}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|5x+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the result using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{14}{5{x}^{2}+16x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|5x+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{5x+1}{x+3}|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the definite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{11}\\frac{14}{5{x}^{2}+16x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{5x+1}{x+3}|{|}_{4}^{11} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "884c56d5f217782d1097ed06237fe2ab45675e0787500cf701f35dd3b22d35a3" "basis" 1560 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d1f4250bdf92c2c10beeab68958ced148fb512341396ca5d2b86210b849b8d1b" "basis" 1560 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75828" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "884c56d5f217782d1097ed06237fe2ab45675e0787500cf701f35dd3b22d35a3" "basis" 1560 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75828" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(12)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "884c56d5f217782d1097ed06237fe2ab45675e0787500cf701f35dd3b22d35a3" "basis" 1560 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75828" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(28)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "884c56d5f217782d1097ed06237fe2ab45675e0787500cf701f35dd3b22d35a3" "basis" 1560 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75828" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2}{3})"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "884c56d5f217782d1097ed06237fe2ab45675e0787500cf701f35dd3b22d35a3" "basis" 1560 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75828" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3})"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "884c56d5f217782d1097ed06237fe2ab45675e0787500cf701f35dd3b22d35a3" "basis" 1560 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75828" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{8}{7})"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "884c56d5f217782d1097ed06237fe2ab45675e0787500cf701f35dd3b22d35a3" "basis" 1560 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75828" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "884c56d5f217782d1097ed06237fe2ab45675e0787500cf701f35dd3b22d35a3" "basis" 1560 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-49762" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{2x+6}{{x}^{2}-4}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069947/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e6e1da2a7764486aa485cdaa8e9685875ceedeb6f36df0e6a8b82f5755aa7d9"} {"question" "q-49762" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We'll work out the indefinite integral first and then proceed with the definite integral.\n\nFirst, we note that a denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-4=(x-2)(x+2).\n$$\n\nSo the integrand can be converted into a sum of partial fractions,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+6}{{x}^{2}-4} & =\\frac{2x+6}{(x-2)(x+2)}=\\frac{A}{(x+2)}+\\frac{B}{(x-2)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n2x+6=A(x-2)+B(x+2).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=2,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(2)+6 & =A(2-2)+B(2+2) \\\\ 10 & =4B \\\\ B & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-2,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-2)+6 & =A(-2-2)+B(-2+2) \\\\ 2 & =-4A \\\\ A & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{2x+6}{{x}^{2}-4}=-\\frac{1}{2(x+2)}+\\frac{5}{2(x-2)}.\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x+6}{{x}^{2}-4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-\\frac{1}{2(x+2)}+\\frac{5}{2(x-2)})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{5}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x-2)^{5}|-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the result using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x+6}{{x}^{2}-4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x-2)^{5}|-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{(x-2)^{5}}{x+2}|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the definite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{2x+6}{{x}^{2}-4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{(x-2)^{5}}{x+2}|{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|-\\frac{1}{3}|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|-{3}^{5}|) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{-1})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{5})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069947/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e6e1da2a7764486aa485cdaa8e9685875ceedeb6f36df0e6a8b82f5755aa7d9"} {"question" "q-49762" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069947/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c00c31d3150c47108bf94460495dad0e183e28d06c73351f89142189f72eea34"} {"question" "q-49762" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069947/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e6e1da2a7764486aa485cdaa8e9685875ceedeb6f36df0e6a8b82f5755aa7d9"} {"question" "q-49762" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] ["math" "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3"] ["math" "-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3"] ["math" "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069947/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e6e1da2a7764486aa485cdaa8e9685875ceedeb6f36df0e6a8b82f5755aa7d9"} {"question" "q-49762" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069947/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e6e1da2a7764486aa485cdaa8e9685875ceedeb6f36df0e6a8b82f5755aa7d9"} {"question" "q-49765" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-7}^{-3}\\frac{11x+46}{(x+2)(x+8)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069947/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e6e1da2a7764486aa485cdaa8e9685875ceedeb6f36df0e6a8b82f5755aa7d9"} {"question" "q-49765" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We'll work out the indefinite integral first and then proceed with the definite integral.\n\nFirst, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{11x+46}{(x+2)(x+8)} & =\\frac{A}{(x+2)}+\\frac{B}{(x+8)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n11x+46=A(x+8)+B(x+2).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-8,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}11(-8)+46 & =A(-8+8)+B(-8+2) \\\\ -42 & =-6B \\\\ B & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-2,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}11(-2)+46 & =A(-2+8)+B(-2+2) \\\\ 24 & =6A \\\\ A & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{11x+46}{(x+2)(x+8)}=\\frac{4}{(x+2)}+\\frac{7}{(x+8)}.\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{11x+46}{(x+2)(x+8)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{4}{x+2}+\\frac{7}{x+8})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x+7\\int \\frac{1}{x+8}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+7\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+8|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n            \n\nWe can simplify the result using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{11x+46}{(x+2)(x+8)}\\,\\text{d}x & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+7\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+8|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x+2)^{4}(x+8)^{7}|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the definite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-7}^{-3}\\frac{11x+46}{(x+2)(x+8)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x+2)^{4}(x+8)^{7}|{|}_{-7}^{-3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({5}^{7})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({5}^{4}) \\\\  & =7\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069947/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e6e1da2a7764486aa485cdaa8e9685875ceedeb6f36df0e6a8b82f5755aa7d9"} {"question" "q-49765" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069947/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c00c31d3150c47108bf94460495dad0e183e28d06c73351f89142189f72eea34"} {"question" "q-49765" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069947/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e6e1da2a7764486aa485cdaa8e9685875ceedeb6f36df0e6a8b82f5755aa7d9"} {"question" "q-49765" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5"] ["math" "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] ["math" "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5"] ["math" "5\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069947/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e6e1da2a7764486aa485cdaa8e9685875ceedeb6f36df0e6a8b82f5755aa7d9"} {"question" "q-49765" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069947/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e6e1da2a7764486aa485cdaa8e9685875ceedeb6f36df0e6a8b82f5755aa7d9"} {"question" "q-75828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate\n${\\int }_{4}^{11}\\frac{14}{5{x}^{2}+16x+3}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069947/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e6e1da2a7764486aa485cdaa8e9685875ceedeb6f36df0e6a8b82f5755aa7d9"} {"question" "q-75828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We'll work out the indefinite integral first and then proceed with the definite integral.\n\nFirst, we note that a denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n5{x}^{2}+16x+3=(5x+1)(x+3).\n$$\n\nSo the integrand can be converted into a sum of partial fractions,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{14}{5{x}^{2}+16x+3} & =\\frac{14}{(5x+1)(x+3)}=\\frac{A}{(5x+1)}+\\frac{B}{(x+3)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n14=A(x+3)+B(5x+1).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-3,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14 & =A(-3+3)+B(5(-3)+1) \\\\ 14 & =-14B \\\\ B & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-\\frac{1}{5},$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14 & =A(-\\frac{1}{5}+3)+B(5(-\\frac{1}{5})+1) \\\\ 14 & =\\frac{14}{5}A \\\\ A & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{14}{5{x}^{2}+16x+3}=\\frac{5}{5x+1}-\\frac{1}{(x+3)}.\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{14}{5{x}^{2}+16x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{5}{5x+1}-\\frac{1}{x+3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{5}{5x+1}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|5x+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the result using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{14}{5{x}^{2}+16x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|5x+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{5x+1}{x+3}|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the definite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{11}\\frac{14}{5{x}^{2}+16x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{5x+1}{x+3}|{|}_{4}^{11} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069947/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e6e1da2a7764486aa485cdaa8e9685875ceedeb6f36df0e6a8b82f5755aa7d9"} {"question" "q-75828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069947/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c00c31d3150c47108bf94460495dad0e183e28d06c73351f89142189f72eea34"} {"question" "q-75828" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069947/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e6e1da2a7764486aa485cdaa8e9685875ceedeb6f36df0e6a8b82f5755aa7d9"} {"question" "q-75828" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(12)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(28)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2}{3})"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3})"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{8}{7})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069947/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e6e1da2a7764486aa485cdaa8e9685875ceedeb6f36df0e6a8b82f5755aa7d9"} {"question" "q-75828" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069947/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e6e1da2a7764486aa485cdaa8e9685875ceedeb6f36df0e6a8b82f5755aa7d9"} {"question" "q-103989" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{2x-4}{x(x-4)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069947/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e6e1da2a7764486aa485cdaa8e9685875ceedeb6f36df0e6a8b82f5755aa7d9"} {"question" "q-103989" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x-4}{x(x-4)} & =\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{x-4},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n2x-4=A(x-4)+Bx.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=4,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(4)-4 & =A(4-4)+B(4) \\\\ 4 & =4B \\\\ 1 & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=0,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(0)-4 & =A(0-4)+B(0) \\\\ -4 & =-4A \\\\ A & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x-4}{x(x-4)} & =\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{x-4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x-4}{x(x-4)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{x-4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069947/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e6e1da2a7764486aa485cdaa8e9685875ceedeb6f36df0e6a8b82f5755aa7d9"} {"question" "q-103989" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069947/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c00c31d3150c47108bf94460495dad0e183e28d06c73351f89142189f72eea34"} {"question" "q-103989" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069947/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e6e1da2a7764486aa485cdaa8e9685875ceedeb6f36df0e6a8b82f5755aa7d9"} {"question" "q-103989" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069947/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e6e1da2a7764486aa485cdaa8e9685875ceedeb6f36df0e6a8b82f5755aa7d9"} {"question" "q-103989" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069947/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e6e1da2a7764486aa485cdaa8e9685875ceedeb6f36df0e6a8b82f5755aa7d9"} {"question" "q-348896" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following indefinite integral and fill in the missing coefficients.\n\n$\\int \\frac{7x+7}{(x+3)(x-4)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|\\,+\\,$\n{{field-2}}$\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069947/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e6e1da2a7764486aa485cdaa8e9685875ceedeb6f36df0e6a8b82f5755aa7d9"} {"question" "q-348896" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n(x+3)(x-4).\n$$\n\nWe convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7x+7}{(x+3)(x-4)} & =\\frac{A}{x+3}+\\frac{B}{x-4},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n7x+7=A(x-4)+B(x+3).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=4,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(4)+7 & =A(4-4)+B(4+3) \\\\ 35 & =7B \\\\ B & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-3,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(-3)+7 & =A(-3-4)+B(-3+3) \\\\ -14 & =-7A \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{7x+7}{(x+3)(x-4)}=\\frac{2}{x+3}+\\frac{5}{x-4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{7x+7}{(x+3)(x-4)}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x+5\\int \\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+5\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069947/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e6e1da2a7764486aa485cdaa8e9685875ceedeb6f36df0e6a8b82f5755aa7d9"} {"question" "q-348896" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069947/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c00c31d3150c47108bf94460495dad0e183e28d06c73351f89142189f72eea34"} {"question" "q-348896" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069947/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e6e1da2a7764486aa485cdaa8e9685875ceedeb6f36df0e6a8b82f5755aa7d9"} {"question" "q-